  "raw": {
    "https://host.pcrecruiter.net/pcrbin/jobboard.aspx?action=detail&recordid=119592017432397&uid=central%20connecticut%20state%20university.centralconnecticutstateuniversity": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Finance",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Finance Back To Results Assistant Professor of Finance Application Deadline November 16, 2026 Full-Time Regular 201541 [C26-039] Assistant Professor Department of Finance Central Connecticut State University (Central) invites applications to join the Finance Department in the School of Business as a full-time, tenure-track Assistant Professor. We seek applicants passionate about preparing the next generation of business professionals by empowering students for success in the workforce. As we recently celebrated 175 years of academic excellence and innovation, we invite you to be a part of our mission at Central. Explore the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the lives of our students and the broader community; please visit Central Connecticut State University to learn more. About Central’s School of Business and Finance Department Central Connecticut State University’s School of Business is an accredited member of AACSB International-The Association of Advance Collegiate Schools of Business. Only six percent of business programs worldwide have attained this prestigious distinction. The School of Business provides high-quality, affordable, and accessible educational programs for undergraduate and graduate students from Central Connecticut and the greater Northeast region. The Finance Department is housed within Central Connecticut State University’s School of Business and is committed to providing students with high-quality, career-focused education that integrates academic knowledge with real-world application. We offer a comprehensive curriculum that includes a Bachelor of Science (B.S.) in Finance with a general finance concentration and a financial planning concentration, as well as a minor in personal financial planning. The B.S. in Finance with financial planning concentration at Central is registered and regulated by the Certified Financial Planner (CFP) Board of Standards, making it the first CFP Board-registered financial planning program in Connecticut. Position Profile This is an exciting opportunity for an individual seeking a rewarding academic career that supports work-life balance and who is passionate about challenging, motivating, and encouraging students in pursuit of their educational and professional goals. The successful candidate will contribute to the department’s commitment to excellence in teaching, research, and student success. Key responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in financial planning and finance, maintaining an active program of scholarly research, supporting student growth and professional development, engaging with the broader community, and serving the department, School of Business, University, and profession. The new hire is expected to be actively involved in our CFP Board-registered financial planning program. Represented by the Connecticut State University American Association of University Professors (CSU-AAUP), full-time faculty enjoy a collegial governance system that embodies the values and principles of shared governance, mutual respect, and professionalism. Applicant Evaluative Criteria Applicant profiles and supplementary materials will be evaluated for appointment based on the following: Education: All applicants must possess a doctoral degree in financial planning or finance or a closely related field from an accredited institution. Special Notes: ABD candidates may be considered upon evidence of anticipated completion by June 30, 2027. Demonstrated record of excellence in teaching in the field of financial planning or finance or a closely related discipline at a college or university. Demonstrated AACSB Scholarly Academic record of current and relevant scholarship and activities related to the field. Experience and Training: Ideal Candidate Preference will be given to applicants with the following: Relevant professional credentials or certifications, such as CFP® certification, JDs, CFA designation, or other recognized credentials in financial planning or finance. Demonstrated substantial professional experience in financial planning, especially in retirement planning, estate planning, wealth management, or a closely related area, with preference for experience at the level of manager or above. Demonstrated evidence of ongoing scholarly activities in the field of financial planning or a closely related discipline. **Candidates who possess a Doctorate or terminal degree plus at least five (5) years of full- time service in a college or university in a rank of Assistant Professor or above or its comparable equivalent may be considered for appointment at the rank of Associate Professor. To Apply To begin the application process, select the “Apply” button and electronically submit the following documents by November 16 th , 2026. Please be sure that you explicitly discuss how your experience and skills match each required and preferred qualification. Please be aware that additional material may be required if selected for interview. Letter of interest addressing the qualifications for this position. Current Résumé Incomplete or late applications will not be considered. E-mailed and mailed applications will not be accepted. Please redact any personally identifiable information (i.e., Social Security Number, date of birth, marital status, country of origin) from any documents submitted. Inquiries may be sent to Dr. Ying Chen, Search Committee Chair, at 860-832-3234 or ying.chen@ccsu.edu . Compensation and Employee Benefits In accordance with the Connecticut State University American Association of University Professors (AAUP) Collective Bargaining Union Contract, compensation for this position is at the rank of Assistant Professor for 2027-2028 [$81,149- $108,199]. Salary is commensurate with education and experience. For more information on the AAUP Collective Bargaining Agreement, please visit AAUP . The State of Connecticut and Central Connecticut State University are proud to offer its employees competitive wages and a wide range of fringe benefits including voluntary and supplemental benefits. Fringe benefits include: paid personal leave and sick leave accruals; medical, dental, and prescription plans; group life insurance; retirement; retiree health care; tuition waiver for employee and eligible dependents at any of the Connecticut State Universities (Central, Eastern, Southern or Western) as well as an array of voluntary and supplemental benefits such as Deferred Retirement Contribution plans, Dependent Care Assistance and Medical Flexible spending accounts; long and short term disability insurance plans. For more detailed information, please visit CCSU Human Resources . As an affirmative action employer, Central Connecticut State University actively seeks and encourages applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. The University provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. Apply Processing..."
    },
    "https://host.pcrecruiter.net/pcrbin/jobboard.aspx?action=detail&recordid=125219375561299&uid=central%20connecticut%20state%20university.centralconnecticutstateuniversity": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of MIS",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of MIS Back To Results Assistant Professor of MIS Application Deadline November 16, 2026 Full-Time Regular 201542 [ C2 6 - 046 ] Assistant Professor of Management Information Systems (MIS) School of Business Central Connecticut State Universit y invites applications to join the Management Information System (MIS) department as a full-time , tenure-track Assistant Professor for the 2027-2028 academic year beginning August 2027 . We seek applicants wh o are student oriented to teach undergraduate and graduate courses. As we recently celebrate d 175 years of academic excellence and innovation, we invite you to be a part of our mission at CCSU. Explore the opportunity to make a meaningful impact on the lives of our students and the broader community, please visit CCSU to learn more. About CCSU’s Management Information Systems Department The Management Information Systems (MIS) department prepares students for careers as business-technology professionals to face challenges in a global transformative environment. The field of Information Systems encompasses data analysis, teamwork, leadership, project management, customer service, and underlying business theories. Technology is an integral part that enables company activities, including management and decision-making. The emphasis of the major is on preparing information specialists in systems, data management, operations, and major business areas. The program emphasizes the importance of timely and quality information as an organizational resource to be managed to assist organizations with decision making. About CCSU’s School of Business The School of Business provides high-quality, affordable, and accessible educational programs for undergraduate and graduate students from Central Connecticut and the greater northeast region. We prepare the next generation of leaders by empowering our students for successful professional futures; developing close relationships with regional businesses; responding to employers’ workforce needs; and promoting faculty excellence in teaching, research, and community engagement. Central’s School of Business is an accredited member of the AACSB International—The Association to Advance Collegiate School of Business. Position Profile The successful candidate will collaborate with faculty, colleagues, and external partners to help students apply technology to complex organizational and societal problems. A central expectation of this position is the ability to develop and teach interdisciplinary courses, modules, and experiential projects that connect information systems, artificial intelligence, analytics, automation, and digital transformation with other business fields, and when appropriate, disciplines outside the School of Business. Applicant Evaluative Criteria Applicant profiles and supplementary materials will be evaluated for appointment based on the following: Education: All applicants must posse s s an advanced degree in Management Information Systems or closely related field from an accredited university. Special Note: ABD Candidates may be considered upon evidence of anticipated completion within one year of hire. Ideal Candidate Preference will be given to applicants with the following: Ph.D. from an AACSB-accredited school Record of successful university teaching Evidence of professional/academic service Experience in Information Technology, Policy and Informatics Programming skills (R, Python, C# or similar) Business analytical skills Ability to develop and teach interdisciplinary courses, modules, and experiential projects To Apply To begin the application process, select the “A pply ” button and electronically submit the following documents by November 16, 2026 . Please be sure that you explicitly discuss how your experience and skills match each required and preferred qualification . Please be aware that additional material may be required if selected for interview . Letter of interest addressing the qualifications for this position . Current R ésumé Incomplete or late applications will not be considered . E- mailed and mailed applications will not be accepted . Please redact any personally identifiable information (i.e., Social Security Number, date of birth, marital status, country of origin) from any documents submitted . Inquiries may be sent to Dr. Michael Gendron , Search Committee Chair, or GendronM@ccsu.edu . Compensation and Employee Benefits In accordance with the Connecticut State University American Association of University Professors (AAUP) Collective Bargaining Union Contract, compensation for this position is at the Assistant Professor rank for 20 2 7 -202 8 [$81,149-$108,199] . Salary is commensurate with education and experience . For more information on the AAUP Collective Bargaining Agreement, please visit AAUP . The State of Connecticut and Central Connecticut State University are proud to offer its employees competitive wages and a wide range of fringe benefits including voluntary and supplemental benefits. Fringe benefits include: paid personal leave and sick leave accruals; medical, dental, and prescription plans; group life insurance; retirement; retiree health care; tuition waiver for employee and eligible dependents at any of the Connecticut State Universities (Central, Eastern, Southern or Western) as well as an array of voluntary and supplemental benefits such as Deferred Retirement Contribution plans, Dependent Care Assistance and Medical Flexible spending accounts; long and short term disability insurance plans. For more detailed information, please visit CCSU Human Resources . As an affirmative action employer, Central Connecticut State University actively seeks and encourages applications from women, minorities, persons with disabilities, and individuals with protected veteran status. The University provides reasonable accommodations to qualified individuals with disabilities upon request. Apply Processing..."
